<DocsLayout title="Observability" description="Understand project telemetry, host telemetry, logs, health signals, and MyPaaS fallback behavior.">
<section><p class="overline">Project telemetry</p><h2>Runtime metrics</h2><p><code>mypaas-statd</code> is optional host-native telemetry. When it is installed and configured, running container-backed projects prefer statd snapshots over its Unix socket. If statd is disabled, unavailable, or cannot provide a usable runtime snapshot, MyPaaS falls back to the metrics path through the Docker-compatible engine contract.</p><DocMedia src={overviewShot} alt="MyPaaS project metrics overview" title="Project runtime metrics" source="MyPaaS dashboard" note="captured 13 Aug 2026" /><aside class="note"><p>Static projects do not have a persistent application runtime and therefore do not expose runtime CPU or memory telemetry.</p></aside></section>
<section><h2>Host telemetry</h2><p>The owner-only host statistics surface keeps host capacity and project allocation separate from live telemetry. With statd v0.2.0 host snapshots, MyPaaS can report host CPU, memory, storage, and network counters without pretending that the API container namespace is the host. Capacity/allocation remain available when live host telemetry is disabled or unavailable.</p><DocMedia src={adminShot} alt="MyPaaS admin resource settings" title="Host and platform settings" source="MyPaaS dashboard" note="captured 13 Aug 2026" /></section>
<section><h2>Project logs</h2><p>Build output remains attached to deployment history. Runtime logs are read through the Docker-compatible command surface, and Compose logs retain service context. <code>mypaas-statd</code> is not the project log collector.</p><DocMedia src={logsShot} alt="MyPaaS project logs view" title="Project logs" source="MyPaaS dashboard" note="captured 13 Aug 2026" /></section>
<section><h2>Control-plane health</h2><p>The API exposes <code>/health</code>, <code>/ready</code>, and Prometheus-compatible <code>/metrics</code>. Production verification checks the statd service/socket when statd is configured and also verifies the Caddy Admin Unix socket.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>/health</code></td><td>Lightweight liveness.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/ready</code></td><td>Readiness and production verification.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/metrics</code></td><td>Control-plane process metrics with production authentication when configured.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section><h2>What the dashboard does not claim</h2><p>MyPaaS does not fabricate historical telemetry from one current percentage. Runtime charts use bounded rolling samples collected while the view is active; host capacity and configured resource allocations remain separate concepts.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>